// The AerialVLA pilot's airframe and cameras (demo/vla_fly.py, mission M1 GOTO).
//
// GENERATED from robot_semantic_quad.jsonc (the same links, joints,
// simple_flight controller, actuators and IMU) with a new camera loadout, so
// the airframe is the one every CityLife flight flew and only the eyes change.
//
// VLAFront and VLADown MATCH AERIALVLA'S TRAINING CAMERAS: 256x256, 90 deg
// FOV, front pitch 0, down pitch -90 (upstream airsim_plugin/settings/30001/
// settings.json, vla-assets discovery report 2026-10-21). The follow rail's
// FrontCamera is 768x432 (16:9) at pitch -20 and its DownCamera 400x225 at
// 2 Hz - a distribution shift for a model trained on square, level views.
// Both are captured every 0.1 s, so the frame behind a decision is at most
// 0.1 s older than the request (one pair per decision is used: the newest of
// each, paired by time in demo/vla_fly.VLAFrames), Scene only, never
// streamed. The server resizes each tile bicubic to 224x224 and stacks front
// over down into the 224x448 mosaic (guardrail/aerialvla_codec.build_mosaic).
//
// Chase (960x540 at 20 Hz) is the third-person view for the video and the
// simulator window; it is the ONLY streaming camera, so the window binds to
// it at load (follow_vlm's --view-switch exists because there a depth stream
// came first; here vla_fly defaults it to 0).
//
// No detector camera: M1's hint comes from the goal, and a 768x432 render
// every 0.1 s on the GPU the model and Unreal share would cost decisions for
// nothing (OWL-ViT ran 13.8-21.5x slower in flight than offline, CHANGELOG).
// robot_vla_quad_det.jsonc adds it for M2.
{
